boomerang (0.8.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New app icon, drawn like elementary's own (series E): a slate iPhone
    tilted behind, the raspberry tile with the white boomerang in front;
    each size drawn on its own pixel grid (data/icon-proposals/install_e5.py).
  * Lighter in the background: the daemon computes its properties once per
    GetAll, indexes the messages cache, follows NetworkManager and obexd by
    their signals, runs no idevice_* or LocalSend work while unused, and
    sends ThreadsChanged only when a listing changed something.
  * Lighter app: a property change runs only the views that show it,
    hidden pages no longer reload, new bubbles are added instead of
    redrawing the conversation, contact photos and artwork are decoded once,
    clocks and polls run only on screen.
  * Panel indicator shows the call in progress again.

 -- melvincouwez-alt <301110918+melvincouwez-alt@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200

boomerang (0.8.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Messages: a conversation opens on its newest message (the scroll
    position was set during an allocation and lost, and GTK's own moves
    while bubbles were laid out were taken for the user scrolling up); the
    list loads once the daemon answers when the window shows first.
  * Per-conversation look (src/ThreadStyle.vala, conversations.conf):
    nickname and emoji, bubble colours, background (tint, gradient or
    picture), text size, bubble shape.
  * Per-conversation notifications kept by boomerangd: priority (banner
    and sound under Do Not Disturb), muted, own sound.
  * Search within the open conversation (Ctrl+F; Ctrl+Shift+F for all),
    a button back to the newest message with a count of new ones, an
    "Unread" line, Alt+Up/Down and Ctrl+N.
  * Optional link previews (off by default; boomerangd/linkpreview.py,
    public addresses only), custom quick replies in Settings and in
    notifications, export of a conversation to PDF or text.
  * The standalone Messages app gets elementary header bars, one per pane.
  * Header bars in Boomerang's colour (raspberry-violet, like Cassette and
    the web apps); a conversation with its own colour tints its header.
  * Backgrounds offered in Personnaliser (data/backgrounds, drawn by
    tools/make_backgrounds.py, plus the system wallpapers) and a default
    look for every conversation in Settings › Messages.
  * The main window has a single header bar with Boomerang's name in the
    middle; the left column folds to icons with dock-style badges, from
    Settings › Display, F9, or by dragging its edge, and keeps its width.
  * Messages: one quick retry when the iPhone refuses the first listing.
  * Notifications: per iPhone app, normal, priority (banner and sound under
    Do Not Disturb) or quiet, its own sound, and its text hidden from the
    banner (GetNotificationAppSettings / SetNotificationAppSettings).
  * Screen mirroring shows in Boomerang's own window (boomerangd/
    mirror_viewer.py: header bar, sized to the picture, full screen with
    F11, its own dock entry); UxPlay hands it the decoded frames through
    shared memory. Needs gstreamer1.0-gtk4 (Recommends), else UxPlay's
    window as before.
  * New Boomerang icon.
  * Contributors page, under Settings in the sidebar: every project,
    library, protocol and sound Boomerang uses or builds on, grouped by
    use, with its authors, what it brings, its license and a link.
  * Experimental head gestures (AlphaFeatures head_gestures): while a call
    rings and AirPods are worn, a nod answers and a shake declines. Head
    tracking packets and the nod/shake detector come from LibrePods
    (AACPManager.kt, GestureDetector.kt), rewritten in Python.
  * Screen mirroring: the screensaver is held off while UxPlay runs
    (-scrsv 1); optional MP4 recording in the Videos folder (-mp4); an
    experimental Bluetooth LE beacon (AlphaFeatures mirror_ble, UxPlay -ble
    with uxplay-beacon) lets the iPhone find the PC without mDNS.

