covalence (0.6.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Calls: the microphone muted for a call is always given back. A late
    mute raced the end-of-call restore and left the default source muted,
    so calls from the PC sent silence; a mark in the state dir also undoes
    a mute left by a stopped daemon.
  * Apple Services: Agenda and Cassette are downloaded from their own
    repositories (melvincouwez-alt/agenda, melvincouwez-alt/cassette), with
    Covalence's releases as a fallback; the row shows the app's version.
  * Translations: OptionalAppRow and seven daemon modules added to POTFILES,
    missing English strings translated, download errors explained.
  * Credits: companion apps in About; Apple trademark notice in
    debian/copyright; SPDX headers completed.

 -- melvincouwez-alt <301110918+melvincouwez-alt@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 04 Oct 2026 20:30:00 +0200

covalence (0.6.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Apple Services: Agenda and Cassette are published with Covalence's
    releases and installed from the tab, checked by their SHA-256. The
    install helper accepts the cassette package.
  * SMS codes: copied to the clipboard as soon as the text arrives, on by
    default (Settings › SMS codes).
  * Calls: quiet mode in Settings › Connection and in the top bar. No ring,
    notification, window or audio taken on the PC; the call stays on the
    iPhone.
  * Icons: Covalence, Messages, Phone, Contacts, Now Playing and Mirror
    redrawn for each size (16 to 64 px installed); iPhone Calendar
    notifications use Agenda's tile.
  * Credits: elementary icons, Inter, LocalSend, UxPlay, libimobiledevice,
    ifuse, libheif and the sounds listed in the README, the site and About;
    debian/copyright covers every icon.

